obo:RO_0002333  a  owl:ObjectProperty .

gomodel:6ac817cf00002250
        a                 owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment      "Comment to reviewer: Scope: GLP-1(7-36) acting on GLP1R in the human pancreatic beta-cell, through Gs, adenylate cyclase, cAMP and PKA to K_ATP channel closure, membrane depolarisation and voltage-gated Ca2+ entry driving insulin secretion.\nChannel cascade: K_ATP indirectly negatively regulates T-type (CACNA1H) and L-type (CACNA1D) channels in parallel, via the membrane potential; both are upstream of P/Q-type (CACNA1A), which triggers exocytosis. The ordering follows the model proposed in the Discussion of PMID:18390794, where the channels are ordered by activation voltage, and is coded IC: no experiment measures the activity of one channel while manipulating another. T-type and L-type channel identities rest on qPCR of human islets (PMID:18390794, online appendix Table 1); the functional experiments used subtype-selective blockers.\n\nNot modelled: voltage-gated Na+ channels (NaV1.6/1.7), which contribute to the action potential upstroke; GIP and glucagon receptor input. Downstream steps were not tested with GLP-1 itself, and several edges are ISS from rodent orthologues.\n\nWill be modeled later: the Epac2 branch of cAMP signalling." ;
        lego:modelstate   "development" ;
        dc:contributor    "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5283-6593" ;
        dc:date           "2026-10-26" ;
        dc:title          "Glucagon-like peptide 1 via GLP1R positively regulates insulin secretion (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy    "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI    gomodel:6ac817cf00002250 ;
        biolink:in_taxon  obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

